const CACHE_NAME = 'bt-sales-v10.48'; // v10.48: fixed two real bugs in Notes & Sheets' formula engine (js/notes-sheets.js), found from a user report that `=sum(a1+a2)` "doesn't work". (1) _nsParseExpr's function-name match (`NAME(args)`) had no case-insensitive flag, so only ALL-CAPS names like =SUM(...) were ever recognized as a function call at all — lowercase/mixed-case (=sum(...), =Sum(...), etc.) silently fell through to #ERR. Regex now matches [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]* (still case-insensitive since _nsCallFn already uppercases the captured name itself). (2) Independently, even correctly-cased =SUM(A1+A2) evaluated to 0: _nsCallFn's numsFrom() helper (used by SUM/AVERAGE/MIN/MAX/COUNT) only recognized a bare range (A1:B2), a bare single cell (A1), or a bare number literal per argument — anything else, including a compound expression like A1+A2 or A1*2, matched none of those three checks and silently contributed nothing. numsFrom() now falls back to evaluating the argument as a real expression (via the same resolveNum() the ROUND/IF/etc functions already use) instead of giving up. Also fixed the same latent bug for pure-number expressions (SUM(5+3) previously returned 5, not 8) by switching the number-literal check to a strict digits-only pattern instead of a bare parseFloat. Verified against a standalone extraction of the engine in Node: =sum(a1+a2), =SUM(A1+A2), =SUM(A1,A2), =SUM(A1:A3), =average(a1,a2), =Sum(A1+A2+A3), =sum(5+3), and an existing =IF(...)/=VLOOKUP(...) case all now return the correct values. Same path, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change — index.html's notes-sheets.js script tag also given a fresh ?v= param since it never had one before. (1) Revived js/bt-search.js (dead code since the AI/commandhub.js removal in v10.33 — see that entry) via new js/global-search.js, a classic script that adds a live fuzzy search box to the top of the existing "All Sections" drawer (js/nav-sections.js): filters that drawer's section/sub-section tree in place (auto-expanding matched branches via nav-sections.js's own BTNavSections._toggle, not a duplicate implementation) and separately fuzzy-ranks the Staff registry (Repository.getStaff()), jumping straight to that employee's Staff Card on tap. index.html: drawer's <h2> renamed "All Sections" -> "Search & Sections", new #gs-input/#gs-staff-results markup added inside its existing .mbody, both ☰-button title/aria-label attrs updated to mention Search, new <script defer src="js/global-search.js"> tag right after nav-sections.js's (load-order matters: it reads window.BTSearch and monkey-patches window.openSectionsDrawer, same layering pattern ui-extras.js already uses on window.showPage). css/nav.css: new .gs-* rules for the search box + result rows. (2) While adding js/global-search.js to APP_SHELL below, noticed js/nav-sections.js and js/nav-recents.js — both real, actively-loaded <script> tags for a while now — were never added here either, same "silently missing offline" class of bug as nearly every entry in this changelog; added both alongside it. (3) Deleted js/ledger-migration.js (migratePettyToLedger) — confirmed via grep zero UI ever called window.migratePettyToLedger (no button, no onclick, nothing); Petty Cash itself (js/manager-petty.js, the mw_petty_ storage keys) is untouched and still fully live, only this unused one-off migration helper is gone. Removed its <script type="module"> tag from index.html and its entry from APP_SHELL below. Verified with `node --check` on the new/changed JS before this bump. — the two files deliberately deferred from batch 5 for their live-binding/monkey-patching concerns. js/conflict-ui.js now imports { EventBus } from event-bus.js and { Repository } from repository.js instead of reading them as bare classic-script globals; reviewConflicts/openConflictModal/_conflictChoose all kept their window bridges since _conflictChoose is called via inline onclick="" on the modal's Keep-This-Device/Keep-Cloud-Version buttons (index.html) and the other two are potential external entry points. js/custom-sections.js now imports loadSalaryMonth from manager-salary.js and { _pettyMonth, _pettyData, _pettyKey, loadPettyMonth } from manager-petty.js — both of those were already real ES modules (converted in earlier batches) exporting real bindings, so this is a straight upgrade from the old "hope the window bridge is fresh" pattern to genuine live module bindings; salaryNextMonth/pettyNextMonth kept their window bridges (called via onclick="" in index.html) and CSEC_KEY kept its bridge too (drive.js/supabase.js still read it as a bare classic-script global). Also fixed a stale load-order comment above manager-page.js's script tag that still claimed jazz-cash.js/custom-sections.js/notes-sheets.js monkey-patch it and that it must stay classic — both claims were already false (v10.9 removed the real patches; custom-sections.js's own header already noted it was never actually a patcher) and the tag itself has said type="module" for several sessions; comment now matches the code. index.html: both script tags flipped from <script defer> to <script type="module">, fresh ?v=20260731a cache-busting params. Verified with node --check on both files. This closes out every file flagged as "queued for a future batch" in v10.45 — module-migration Stage B has no known remaining blocked files, only files nobody has gotten to yet. // v10.45: module-migration Stage B, batch 5 — six more classic scripts converted to real ES modules: js/rules-engine.js (no deps, trivial), js/rules-registrations.js (already fully window.-qualified, just unwrapped its IIFE), js/diff-report.js (now `import { MONTHLY, n, fc } from './config.js'`, was reading them off config.js's temporary window bridge), js/index-page.js (now imports `{ n, fc, ff }` from config.js; Analytics stays a bare identifier since analytics.js itself isn't converted yet), js/nav-recents.js (now `import { EventBus } from './event-bus.js'` instead of a `typeof EventBus !== 'undefined'` guard; also swapped its bare `_curPage` read for storage.js's real `getCurrentPage()` bridge, since a module can't rely on classic-script shared scope the way another classic script can), js/targets.js (now imports Repository/Actions/{MONTHLY,n,fc}). Every function still called from inline onclick="" attributes or as a bare global by not-yet-converted classic scripts (ui.js, app-init.js, index.html's own onclick handlers) keeps its existing window bridge — same non-negotiable rule as every prior batch (v10.5 through v10.9's notes below). index.html's six script tags flipped from `<script defer>` to `<script type="module">`, each with a fresh `?v=20260731a` cache-busting param. No consumer-side changes needed in ui.js/app-init.js/dashboard-insights.js/manager-export.js — they all already used bare-identifier/typeof-guarded/window.-qualified calls into these six files, which keep working unchanged against the window bridges. Verified with `node --check` on all six files before this bump. Still queued for a future batch (deliberately left alone — messier monkey-patching/live-binding concerns, noted here so it isn't lost): conflict-ui.js, custom-sections.js. // v10.44: Sales section — new hero card at the very top of Cover's Sales group (js/cover-dashboard.js's new _monthSaleBreakdown(), rendered via monthSaleCard()) breaking the latest month's TOTAL down into how it was actually collected: Cash, Banks, Cash & Banks combined, Credit Clients (including free issue/F-Issue), and Customers — reuses config.js's existing mBanks()/creditSales()/negR() helpers (already custom-field-aware) so this can never drift from what Dashboard/Reports already compute for the same month. Falls back to the latest MONTHLY record (same convention as the existing _salesStatus()) if the current calendar month has no entries yet; renders nothing if MONTHLY is empty. css/cover-dashboard.css got 5 new .ccs-stat.ccs-cash/ccs-bank/ccs-cashbank/ccs-credit/ccs-cust icon-background rules, reusing the existing Latest Closing Summary stat-grid markup/classes (.ccs-stat-grid/.ccs-stat/.ccs-ic/.ccs-lbl/.ccs-val) rather than inventing a new pattern. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. // v10.43: Reorder Report (js/reorder-report.js) — whether today's live sales fold into the 30/60/90-day sale qty/value used for filtering/ranking/demand calc is now a UI toggle ("+ Today" / "Historical Only" in the filter row, both tabs), not fixed on. Previously always-on folding could drift from Candela's own C-19 report (historical-window-only); "Historical Only" now reproduces that exactly on demand, "+ Today" (still the default, same as before this change) keeps the live demand signal for day-to-day buying. computeAllRows() takes a new includeToday param (state.includeToday, persisted as bt_reorder_includetoday_v1); when off, saleQty/saleValue/daysCover/demandQty per window reduce to the pure historical figures and effectiveDays drops the todayFraction term. "Sold Today" column is unaffected either way — always real today's activity, informational only. getSummaryFor() (Cover Dashboard's fixed stat) gained the same param but keeps defaulting to true regardless of this page's own toggle, so visiting/changing Reorder Report's controls still never moves Cover's number, same independence guarantee as its window/coverDays/topN params already had. Same path, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. // v10.42: Reorder Report (js/reorder-report.js) — Sale Value (saleValueP/saleValue{w}/saleValueToday, and every total built on them: group subtotals, Cover Dashboard's getSummaryFor, exports) always read the *_excl_tax field from inventory_products regardless of the product's own isTaxable flag. Exempt items (e.g. Panadol) were unaffected since their incl/excl fields are identical, but taxable items understated their real sale value by the VAT amount. computeAllRows() now picks *_incl_tax for taxable rows and *_excl_tax for exempt rows (isTaxable-driven field selection, no change to the underlying server-side qty/pack/discount math). Sale Value column in the table now shows "incl. tax"/"no tax" under the figure per row so which basis applies is never ambiguous. Same path, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. // v10.41: BT Inventory (inventory-native.js/index.html/inventory-native.css) — the bridge (inventory-bridge.js) already mapped every inventory_products column as of the 2026-07-30 fix, but the table itself still only ever rendered 6 of them (Product/Qty/Price/Manufacturer/Supplier/Conv.). Added a "☰ Columns" picker (new #bti-columns-btn/#bti-columns-panel in index.html) listing the remaining ~16 columns (creation/last-receive/last-sale dates, net qty + sale value incl/excl tax for 30/60/90-day and Today windows, tax %/isTaxable), grouped and individually toggleable via checkboxes, off by default so the base table stays compact. Selection persists across sessions (bt_biColumns_v1, Repository-first/localStorage-fallback, same pattern as reorder-report.js's settings keys) — data itself was always fully loaded via the bridge already, this only changes what's rendered. Extra <th>/<td> are inserted/removed dynamically (#bti-thead-row + .bti-extra-th/.bti-extra-td) rather than hand-listing every column in static HTML; group-header colspan updated to account for the current extra-column count. No changes to inventory-bridge.js, stockledger.js, or reorder-report.js in that pass — those were already correct then (bridge maps all ~23 columns, Stock Ledger's normalizeSupabaseRow does too); reorder-report.js's own tax-field bug (fixed above in v10.42) was found in a later pass. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. // v10.40: fixed the "already added" receipt (bt_closing_ledger_marks) silently getting lost when its Supabase write failed (dropped connection / expired session mid-write — Credit Ledger showed "✓ Added — but the marker failed to save"). Root cause: closing-ledger-marks.js's saveMark() only ever held the mark in an in-memory map; a failed upsert left nothing behind, so getMark() kept returning null and the row could flip back to showing "+ Ledger" — tapping it again would silently create a second, duplicate real ledger entry (the actual harm the old toast copy warned about but didn't prevent). Fix: saveMark() now (1) updates the in-memory _marks map optimistically before attempting the write, so the row reads as Added for the rest of the session even if the write fails, and (2) on failure, stashes the pending row in a new localStorage-backed queue (bt_pending_ledger_marks_v1) instead of dropping it. fetchMarks() merges any still-queued rows into its result on every load (so a reload doesn't lose the Added state either) and kicks off a background retry; a new flushPendingMarks() export retries every queued row against Supabase and is also wired to the window 'online' event, so reconnecting retries automatically. ledger-quick-add.js's two mark-failure toasts updated to match ("receipt will finish syncing in the background" instead of the old "may still show + Ledger" warning, which is no longer accurate). Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change.
// v10.37: found and removed the ACTUAL left-edge colour strip (js/ui-extras.js's #uex-strip) — v10.36's border-left removal on .cover-group cards was a real but separate cosmetic fix; this is the always-on, page-independent 8px vertical band (Dashboard/Sales/Manager/Tools segments, each a solid color, expanding to show icon+label on hover) that js/ui-extras.js built once on DOMContentLoaded and kept alive across every page via document.body.appendChild — invisible to a plain grep for CSS files since its styles were injected via a runtime <style> tag (_injectStyles()) rather than living in any .css file, which is why it wasn't caught investigating v10.36's request. Confirmed via its hover-tooltip text ("Dashboard  (click to open)", exact match found via grep across all JS) against a screenshot showing that exact string. Removed entirely: the TABS/PAGE_GROUP definitions, _buildEdgeStrip()/_updateStrip(), the #uex-strip/.uex-seg/.uex-icon/.uex-lbl block inside _injectStyles(), and every call site (_init()'s _buildEdgeStrip()+initial _updateStrip() detection, _patchShowPage()'s per-navigation _updateStrip() call). Confirmed via grep that nothing else in the file or the rest of the repo referenced any of it. Left untouched: the floating Dashboard FAB (Ctrl+D), self-heal-targets-on-Tools-open, and the rest of _patchShowPage()'s wrapping — none of them depended on the strip. The permanent ☰ button + All Sections sidebar (v10.36) already covers this strip's own navigation purpose across every page, not just the 4 tabs this one knew about.gether. (1) Removed the colored left border strip from every .cover-group card (css/cover-dashboard.css) — the per-group accent color still drives the icon bubble/title text, just not a solid 4px stripe down the left edge. (2) Added a permanent ☰ button fixed to the left edge of every page (index.html/.side-menu-btn) that opens the existing "All Sections" drawer (js/nav-sections.js) — previously reachable ONLY via a 500ms long-press on the Cover bottom-nav item, which still also works. That drawer is now docked as a real full-height left sidebar (slide-in animation) instead of the generic centered-desktop/bottom-sheet-mobile modal shell every other .mbg uses, scoped via #sectionsbg so nothing else changed shape. (3) Cover's own dashboard cards (Inventory/Manager/Closing/Sales/Audit/...) are now drag-to-reorder via a small ⠿ handle in each header (pointer events, mouse+touch in one path) — new bt_cover_order_v1 Repository key (js/cover-dashboard.js, mirrors the existing pin/collapse persistence pattern exactly), read by a new _orderedGroupNames() that renderCoverDashboard() now iterates instead of the old fixed GROUP_ORDER array (GROUP_ORDER itself is untouched, still the permanent full-set/reconciliation source). The All Sections drawer mirrors this same order for its own top-level rows (per explicit request) via each bnav-item's existing data-domain-group attribute — already used by nav.css's domain-isolation rules — mapped onto Cover's group slugs; items with no domain-group (Cover itself, Tools, PDF Library) keep a fixed position (Cover always pinned first), and every sub-section row (Sale Data's tabs, Manager's tabs, Credit Ledger's mode tabs) stays in fixed original order, never reordered, exactly as requested. New window.btGetCoverOrder() bridge (cover-dashboard.js is a real ES module; nav-sections.js is a classic script and can't import it directly). index.html/css bumped: nav.css, cover-dashboard.css, cover-dashboard.js, nav-sections.js all ?v=20260728a. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change.taff Credit entirely — its Ledger dropdown only listed getAllLedgerTypes() (Jazz Cash/Expense/Petty/custom "Other Sections"), but Staff Credit predates the generalized Ledger and isn't one of those (see manager-credit.js's header) — so a Closing Credit Ledger "tier" row (e.g. a named staff member) had nowhere correct to go. Fixed by giving Staff Credit its own branch throughout the modal: a "👥 Staff Credit" option prepended to the Ledger dropdown; selecting it swaps the Category dropdown for a Staff dropdown (from manager-staff.js's activeStaff(), always blank by default — same "human confirms every time" rule as everything else in this modal, no auto-matching against the row's own label even though that name is sitting right there); on Save it resolves the correct month from the ROW'S OWN DATE (not "current month" — a Closing row from last month must land in last month's sheet), via manager-credit.js's exported _crdData(monthKey), pushes a {date, desc, amount, source:'closing_app'} entry (source tag already renders the 📱 Closing badge in manager-credit.js's entryRowsFor, same convention as the Ledger's own entries), and saves via manager-shared.js's mgrLoad/mgrSave — the same underlying store manager-credit.js's own Save button and quick-add.js's pre-existing (Manager-page-only) Staff Credit quick-add both write to, just resolved by date instead of by whichever month happens to be open in the UI. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change.
// v10.34 (superseded above): fixed Credit Ledger date-cards auto-collapsing every ~15s. Root cause: closing-bridge.js polls Closing's exported data every MIN_REFRESH_MS (15s, recently dropped from 5min for near-real-time cross-device sync) and fully rebuilds Credit Ledger's HTML on every poll (js/closing-native.js's renderCreditLedgerPage), but expand/collapse state lived ONLY as a CSS 'open' class on the DOM element — nothing tracked it in JS — so every 15s poll silently reset every open card back to closed. Pre-existing bug, unrelated to the v10.33 Quick Add feature (just became far more noticeable once the poll interval dropped to 15s). Fix: clState (already used for filter/visibleCount) now also holds an `expanded` Set of "mode:date" keys; clToggleDateCard/clToggleAll update both the DOM class and the set; clBuildDateCard/mlBuildDateCard read the set back on every render (via a new data-key attribute) so a rebuild restores whatever was open instead of resetting it. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. v10.33: Credit Ledger → real Ledger "Quick Add" wiring. New files js/ledger-quick-add.js (manual add-entry modal, opened per-row from Closing's native Credit Ledger view — date/shift/amount/description pre-filled from the row, Ledger + Category always left blank for the user to pick, writes via the existing LedgerActions.addEntry door, source:'closing_app' so it carries the already-existing 📱 Closing badge in ledger-page.js) and js/closing-ledger-marks.js (thin wrapper around a new standalone Supabase table, bt_closing_ledger_marks — a receipt/audit trail of which Closing rows already got added, nothing more; not part of the real ledger data and not read by anything that writes real financial data). closing-native.js: clBuildShiftBlock's row renderer now shows a "+ Ledger" button per Named/Staff-Tier/Free-Entry line, or a struck-through "✓ Added" badge if a mark already exists for that row (row identity = snapshot key + immutable line index, since saved-snapshot lines carry no id of their own and are never re-ordered after a shift closes); onShowCreditLedger fetches marks async and re-renders once loaded. supabase.js: one new window.btGetSupabaseClient() getter so the two new ES modules can reuse the existing authenticated client instead of duplicating SB_URL/SB_KEY. css/closing-native.css: .cl-qa-btn/.cl-added-badge/.cl-line-added + .cl-line-right wrapper rules. This is explicitly NOT a revival of the old auto-sync/inbox model removed per request (bt_inbox_ledger etc, see bt-bridge.js's header) — every field a human didn't type is either an unambiguous fact copied from the row (date/shift/amount/description) or left blank for a human to choose (ledger/category); nothing writes without an explicit Save tap. — every AI-facing feature is gone: the Hub/CommandHub chat page and its nav tab/bottom-nav entry, AI Settings (Groq/Gemini/Cerebras keys), Instructions & Memory (Knowledge Base sheet), the Context Engine (active-context strip), the AI Daily Briefing card on Cover, and the whole js/ai/ provider+domain-registry subsystem underneath all of it. Deleted outright (20 JS + 5 CSS files, all real, verified-zero-remaining-consumer via grep before each deletion): js/ai-bridge.js, ai-context.js, ai-context-ui.js, ai-helpers.js, ai-instructions.js, ai-instructions-ui.js, commandhub.js, commandhub-page.js, hub-actions.js, knowledge-sheet.js, app-context.js, intent-groups.js, the entire js/ai/ folder (core/ai-briefings.js, ai-client.js, ai-datetime.js, ai-memory.js, ai-providers.config.js, registry.js, domains/inventory-domain.js, manager-domain.js, sales-domain.js), css/ai-context.css, ai-instructions.css, assistant.css, assistant-fixes.css, intent-groups.css. index.html: removed the Hub nav tab, the entire #page-commandhub markup block (chat thread, context strip, settings/memory modals, scan input), and every <script>/<link> tag for the files above. Edited (not deleted) to drop only their AI/Hub-specific pieces, everything else in each file untouched: js/cover-dashboard.js (Daily Briefing import/card/click-handler, Hub quick-access tile), js/nav-recents.js + nav-sections.js + ui-extras.js (Hub nav-tab entries), js/ui.js (commandhub page-init dispatch + active-tab highlighting), js/actions.js (three now-orphaned storage helpers: saveAiInstructions/saveAiMemoryItem/saveCommandHubRecents — verified zero remaining callers before removal), js/boot-guard.js (stale module-list mention in its own error message). Left deliberately untouched: roughly a dozen files (actions.js, app-context.js's former "consumed by" comments now pointing at nothing, bt-date.js, bt-format.js, bt-search.js, index-page.js, ledger-actions.js, manager-*.js, notes-sheets.js, print.js, targets.js) still carry pure-documentation comments/window-bridges naming the now-deleted files as historical consumers — confirmed via grep that none of these are real function calls (the dependency direction was always AI/Hub reading FROM these files, never the reverse), so they're inert, not broken; a future pass can reword the comments but nothing here needed a functional change. Cash Deposit thermal receipt, TOTAL row — the v10.30 vector rewrite fixed every line except TOTAL, which still showed garbled/spaced-out digits cut off at the page edge on a real device ("¨ 6 9 6 ,"). Root cause: jsPDF's built-in Courier/Helvetica fonts are WinAnsi-only and have no glyph for ₨ (U+20A8, only TOTAL used it — every other row's value is plain digits/minus sign, which is why only TOTAL broke). Confirmed against the real jsPDF@2.5.1 build: hitting ₨ mid-string doesn't just drop the character, it silently switches that whole text() call to a 2-byte-per-character encoding the standard font can't decode (visible as alternating null bytes in the raw PDF content stream — matches the "spaced-out digit" look exactly), and the resulting mis-measured string width pushes the right-aligned text off the page edge. Fixed by using plain ASCII "Rs " instead of "₨" for that one PDF-drawn value (js/cash-deposit-report.js's totalValue) — the in-app HTML preview elsewhere in the same file keeps ₨ since browsers handle Unicode normally; this only affects text that goes through jsPDF's own text()/autoTable() calls. Re-verified the same way as v10.30: extracted every text operator from a real generated PDF (all 51 tokens present, TOTAL's "Rs" and "1,276,425" now separate clean tokens instead of one garbled blob) and rendered to PNG via poppler to confirm visually. index.html bumped js/cash-deposit-report.js to ?v=20260727a alongside this. Cash Deposit thermal receipt — replaced the html2canvas-captured HTML template with a vector jsPDF+autoTable renderer (new Print.renderThermalTable() in js/print.js; js/cash-deposit-report.js now builds a plain-data spec instead of an HTML string). This report's html2canvas path had been patched four separate times (v10.21-v10.24) for a clipped/missing value column, and the latest real-device report showed the title text itself clipped too — each prior patch was a real, verified html2canvas/CSS bug, but they kept recurring, so removing html2canvas from this path entirely removes that whole class of bug rather than chasing a fifth CSS theory. Verified with the real jsPDF@2.5.1 + jspdf-autotable@3.8.2 packages (matching index.html's CDN pins) in Node: extracted every text-drawing operator from the actual generated PDF's content stream and confirmed all 50 expected tokens (every label/value across 4 real day-blocks, TOTAL, footer) are present, then rendered it to a PNG via poppler and visually confirmed a single page with nothing clipped top/bottom/left/right. Caught and fixed one real bug in the process: autoTable defaults to a ~20mm bottom margin, which silently pushed the TOTAL row onto a phantom second page since the custom-height page this builds has no such margin — fixed via an explicit `margin.bottom: 0` (the page height is already computed to fit the content exactly, in a first throw-away-page measurement pass). index.html bumped js/print.js to ?v=20260726e and js/cash-deposit-report.js to ?v=20260726e alongside this. fixed "AI call failed: gemini 404" — js/ai/core/ai-providers.config.js's text entry was pinned to 'gemini-2.5-flash', which Google has since retired in favor of 'gemini-3.6-flash' (shipped July 21, 2026); updated the model ID. Also closed a real robustness gap this exposed in js/ai/core/ai-client.js's _isRetryable(): a 404 (model not found/retired) was NOT in the retryable set, so a single stale model ID killed the whole callAI() chain immediately instead of falling through to the next configured provider (Cerebras, if a key were set) — 404 added alongside the existing 400/429/model_decommissioned checks. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change. v10.28: added a Gemini API key field to the ⚙ AI Settings panel (js/commandhub-page.js) — same treatment as the existing Cerebras fallback field (masked display, Free-key link to aistudio.google.com/app/apikey, Remove link, saved/cleared via the existing generic aiSaveProviderKey('gemini', ...) bridge — no new bridge functions needed, only chpClearGeminiSettings added + window-bridged to match chpClearCerebrasSettings's existing convention). Same path, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change — version bumped purely so already-installed clients refetch the new field instead of only seeing Groq/Cerebras forever. v10.27: added Gemini as a free fallback text provider (js/ai/core/ai-providers.config.js — new entry between Groq and Cerebras, using Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint) + a matching note in js/ai/core/ai-client.js's header comment about setting its key via console until the Settings panel grows a field. Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, content-only change — version bumped purely so already-installed clients refetch the new provider entry instead of running the Groq/Cerebras-only list forever. v10.26: added js/ai/core/ai-briefings.js — new AI Daily Briefing hero card on Cover (Sales/Manager/Inventory one-liners, cached per calendar day, background-regenerated via the existing callAI() provider chain). Only ever reached via `import` from cover-dashboard.js (same as ai-client.js/ai-datetime.js/ai-memory.js — no <script> tag needed), so it must still be listed in APP_SHELL below or an already-installed client's SW never fetches it and the import 404s offline. cover-dashboard.js (new import + briefing row, prepended to container.innerHTML ahead of the existing group rows) and css/cover-dashboard.css (.cover-ai-briefing-* rules) both changed in place — same paths, already in APP_SHELL, nothing to add there. v10.25: this session's changes had never bumped this file — same "silently stale on already-installed clients" class of bug as every other entry in this changelog, just caught before anyone had to report it as its own symptom. Real content changed in: js/cover-dashboard.js (added, then on follow-up request removed, four Cover charts — net effect vs v10.24 is Sales-by-Weekday only), js/ledger-page.js (date-range filter + group-by-category on every Ledger view — Patty/Expenses, Jazz Cash, custom sections), js/analytics.js + js/dashboard.js (Overview's Patty/Expenses card gets its own independent date filter plus per-category expand-to-entries, via a new optional dateFrom/dateTo on _ledgerBreakdown()/getCreditSectionData() — every other Overview card stays all-time/unaffected). index.html's script tags for all four bumped their own `?v=` alongside this (cover-dashboard.js/analytics.js/dashboard.js already had one; ledger-page.js never had one before now). Also: since this bump repackages the cache fresh, it carries v10.24's already-committed Cash Deposit thermal-receipt fix along with it for any client whose tab was still open (and therefore still running the pre-v10.24 SW/content) when that fix first shipped — if the missing-value-column symptom is still visible after this reaches you, fully close the tab/app (not just refresh) and reopen once, so the new SW actually takes over before the next paint.
// v10.24: Cash Deposit thermal receipt — found and empirically verified the ACTUAL cause of the missing value column (v10.21-v10.23 fixed real but secondary bugs: caching, host clipping, flex-vs-inline-block — none were it). Reproduced the exact bug offline using a real headless-Chromium + the exact html2canvas 1.4.1 build from cdnjs (matching index.html's CDN version) against the exact committed template: a plain single-span <div> showing the day's date, sitting immediately before the rows wrapper inside each day-block, reliably made html2canvas drop the FIRST row's value span specifically (Cash Sale's number vanished on every day block while Cash Returns/FDPP POS/FDPP Consumer/Cash to Deposit/TOTAL all rendered correctly) — confirmed by removing/emptying that date div (fixes it), reordering rows (bug stays with position 1, not the Cash Sale label), and swapping monospace/flex/inline-block (none of it mattered). Fixed by giving the date header the same two-span row structure as every working line() row (with a genuinely empty, non-fv()'d second span) instead of a plain text div — verified end-to-end against the real function, both days, TOTAL row, before committing. index.html's cash-deposit-report.js bumped to ?v=20260726c alongside this version bump.
// v10.23: Cash Deposit thermal receipt — found the REAL cause of the missing value column after v10.22's cache fix let the actual current code finally reach a client and show the bug clearly: js/cash-deposit-report.js's line() helper and the TOTAL row both used display:flex;justify-content:space-between to right-align the numeric value against the label. flexbox alignment properties are a known html2canvas weak spot (the capture engine print.js hands this HTML to) — the label span painted fine but the space-between-positioned value span routinely got measured with zero width / painted outside its box, which is exactly what v10.21/v10.22 were chasing without ever finding this specific cause (the earlier comment in that file blamed table/grid layout and switched to flex, which turned out to have the identical flaw for this specific case). Fixed by replacing both with explicit-width (62/38 and 55/45) plain inline-block columns — no flex at all — which html2canvas measures reliably. index.html's cash-deposit-report.js script tag bumped to ?v=20260726b as the second safety net alongside this version bump, same two-layer reasoning as v10.22.
// v10.22: Cash Deposit thermal/PDF print — the last two commits changed js/print.js twice (moving the html2canvas capture host from off-screen positioning to opacity:0-in-viewport, then fixing the actual root cause: variables.css's site-wide overflow-x:hidden on html/body was clipping the wider-than-viewport capture host at the phone's real screen width, dropping the header/value column/footer off the printed receipt) but never bumped this version — so already-installed clients kept serving the stale cached print.js through both fixes, which is why the printed output looked byte-for-byte unchanged after a hard refresh. print.js was already correctly listed in APP_SHELL below since v10.1; the file path never needed to change, only this version number, to force already-installed clients to actually refetch its new content instead of holding the old cached copy indefinitely.
// v10.21: Cash to be Deposited report — two follow-up fixes on top of the earlier push that added this feature. (1) APP_SHELL below was missing css/cash-deposit-report.css and js/cash-deposit-report.js — both real, actively-loaded files (index.html's own <link>/<script> tags for them were already correct) — same "silently missing offline" class of bug as every other entry in this changelog; added both now, in their real index.html load positions (css after pdf-library.css, js right after reports.js). (2) UI tweak: the day list's checkbox/total/"Generate Report" bar (#cdr-selbar) moved from below the table to above it, sticky-top instead of sticky-bottom, so it's visible without scrolling past the (often long) day list first — index.html and css/cash-deposit-report.css both updated; js/cash-deposit-report.js itself is unchanged (it already sorted the day list latest-on-top from the earlier push, and doesn't reference the bar's position). Version bumped so already-installed clients actually fetch the corrected shell list + the repositioned bar instead of keeping the old ones cached forever.
// v10.20: Cover page — every group header (Sales/Manager/Notes & Sheets/Closing/Audit/Inventory/Reports) now shows a live one-line subtitle under its title (js/cover-dashboard.js's new _groupSubtitle(), reusing each domain's existing hero-card data helper so the collapsed teaser can never disagree with the expanded view — target pace, outstanding credit, most-recent pinned note, latest closing summary, open audit engagements, total/negative inventory value, and the 3 Reports links respectively). Also: all cover groups now default to collapsed on a client's very first load (new ALL_GROUP_SLUGS seed in _getCollapsed() — only applies once; any real stored user preference, even an empty array meaning "everything expanded", still wins). css/cover-dashboard.css got new .cover-group-head-text/.cover-group-subtitle rules for the stacked title+subtitle block. index.html's cover-dashboard.css link and cover-dashboard.js script tag both got fresh ?v= cache-busting params (same two-layer reasoning as v10.11's note below — CacheStorage version bump here + the HTTP-cache-busting query param are independent safety nets, both needed). Version bumped so already-installed clients refetch the changed CSS/JS instead of serving the cached v10.19 copies.

// v10.17: Load-every-table-into-Sheets — Notes & Sheets' 🔗 Data tab now covers all three domains (Sales/Manager/Inventory), not just Sales: a new Domain dropdown picks Sales/Manager/Inventory, a Table dropdown picks the specific source (Manager: Staff/Salary/Generic Working/Credit Ledger/Petty Cash/Incentive/Unmatched; Inventory: BT Inventory/Stock Ledger Raw/Excess Stock/Reorder Flagged), and a new "📥 Send to Sheets" button materializes whatever's showing (full filtered set, up to 5000 rows) into a brand-new editable grid in the same bt_sheet_workbooks_v1 storage every other sheet already uses — no new backend, rides entirely on existing sync. Also reworked "⬆ Import XLSX" into "⬆ Import Workbook": it now reads every worksheet tab in the picked file (not just the first) into its own grid inside one new file, instead of overwriting whatever grid was already open. Small additive exports needed to read Manager's live data as real ES imports (no window-bridge polling): manager-incentive.js now exports INCEN_PFX/_INC_FIELDS/_incData/_incMonth, manager-unmatched.js now exports unmatchedLoad — both previously module-private. reorder-report.js gained a new getFlaggedRows() export (it only exposed summary stats before) so Reorder Report's actual rows, not just totals, can be read live. No circular imports (verified via grep before adding any of this: none of manager-salary.js/manager-generic.js/manager-credit.js/manager-petty.js/manager-incentive.js/manager-unmatched.js/inventory-bridge.js import notes-sheets.js, directly or transitively). Same paths, already in APP_SHELL below (notes-sheets.js, manager-incentive.js, manager-unmatched.js, reorder-report.js) — nothing to add there; version bumped purely so already-installed clients refetch the changed content instead of running the old Sales-only Data tab forever. // v10.15: PDF Library popup rework — print.js no longer opens a blank "Generating…" tab up front and silently auto-saves to Downloads on completion; instead js/print.js's _generateAndDeliver() calls window.PdfLibrary.beginPrint() the instant a print is requested (shows one popup immediately, "Generating…" state, owned by pdf-library.js) then window.PdfLibrary.finishPrint({blob, filename, title}) once the blob exists (swaps the SAME popup to View / Download / Save-to-Library — no forced tab, no silent download; View/Download are real clicks inside an already-open popup so they're never popup-blocked). window.PdfLibrary.failPrint(err) closes the popup instead of leaving it stuck on "Generating…" if PDF generation throws. print.js's old _reservePreviewTab()+auto-doc.save() combo is kept only as a fallback for the (should-never-happen) case where pdf-library.js isn't loaded. captureFromPrint (the old, save-prompt-only entry point) is gone, replaced by beginPrint/finishPrint/failPrint. No new files — both js/print.js and js/pdf-library.js changed in place, css/pdf-library.css got new .pl-gen-state/.pl-spinner/.pl-quick-actions rules for the new "Generating…" and quick-view/download states — same paths, already in APP_SHELL below, so nothing to add there; version bumped purely so already-installed offline clients refetch the changed file content instead of running the old two-tabs-plus-a-modal flow forever (same reasoning as v10.13's changed-content-only bump). v10.14: PDF Library — new in-app, cross-device library of every PDF the app generates, hung off the one central hook every report already funnels through (js/print.js's _generateAndDeliver()). New files: css/pdf-library.css + js/pdf-library.js (save-category/expiry prompt shown on every print, Supabase Storage upload + bt_pdf_library metadata row, silent expiry sweep on boot via auth.js's unlockApp(), and the #page-pdf-library list/search/filter/view/download UI) — both added to APP_SHELL below in their real index.html load positions (css after reorder-report.css, js right after supabase.js, since pdf-library.js's lazy _getClient() only needs supabase-js's UMD global to exist by the time it's actually called, not at parse time). Same "silently missing offline" class of bug as every changelog entry below if these aren't added here — the file exists on the server the moment it's deployed, but an already-installed client's SW won't know to fetch it until this version bump forces the self-heal/precache pass. No existing files' cache entries changed. v10.13: Petty Cash — added a "🖨 Print Group" button to every petty group's footer (js/manager-petty.js), wired to a new printPettyGroup(gi) that reuses the same _pettyGroupBlockHTML() markup as the existing full-month printPettyReport(), so single-group and full-report prints can't drift apart. The button is rendered inside renderPettyGroups()'s per-group template, so any group added later via addPettyGroup() gets it automatically — no per-group wiring needed. No new files, existing script tag/APP_SHELL entry unchanged; version bumped only so already-installed offline clients refetch the changed file. v10.12: Phase 5 domain-registry split (AI + CommandHub Build Plan v2) — added js/ai/core/registry.js, js/ai/core/ai-datetime.js, js/ai/domains/manager-domain.js, js/ai/domains/sales-domain.js (all new, real ES modules, all real <script type="module"> imports). Also fixed three pre-existing APP_SHELL gaps, same "silently missing offline" class of bug as every entry below: js/ai/core/ai-client.js and js/ai/core/ai-providers.config.js (added in the Phase 0 provider-layer work, never added here) and js/ai/domains/inventory-domain.js (added in the Phase 2 inventory-domain work, never added here) were all real, actively-loaded files missing from this list. Separately, js/ai-memory.js moved to js/ai/core/ai-memory.js (folder-structure cleanup, matches its sibling ai-client.js/ai-providers.config.js) — index.html's script tag and this file's entry both updated to the new path; the old js/ai-memory.js path will 404 on already-installed clients until they pick up this cache-name bump, same reasoning as v10.5's bt-calc.js removal. Also deleted three confirmed-dead files that were never actually removed from disk despite earlier changelog entries claiming so: js/manager.js (1906-line monolith, superseded since v10.8's manager-*.js split — not loaded by any <script> tag), js/data-base.js (v10.9 claimed deleted, wasn't), js/bt-calc.js (v10.5 claimed deleted, wasn't) — none of the three were ever in APP_SHELL, so no entries to remove here, just noting for the record. v10.11: added Reorder Report (Audit domain) — js/reorder-report.js + css/reorder-report.css, both missing from APP_SHELL below (same "silently missing offline / never actually updates on already-installed clients" class of bug as v10.1/v10.2/v10.3's fixes — this file's own CACHE_NAME is the only thing that makes an already-installed client notice new/changed same-origin files at all, since networkFirst still needs a controlling SW that knows to run it; a content change to sw.js with no version bump doesn't reliably trigger the browser's SW update check on every client). Root symptom this fixes: Reorder Report showed "0 items pulled" from Stock Ledger on an already-installed client even after redeploying js/stockledger.js's new getRawRows() bridge — the already-running SW/tab never re-fetched it. index.html's own script/link tags also got a `?v=` query param in this same deploy as a second, independent safety net (browser HTTP cache, distinct from this file's CacheStorage) — both are needed since either one alone can serve stale files. v10.10: fixed "JC_KEY is not defined" breaking Supabase Pull and Google Drive Backup on every run. Root cause: jazz-cash.js was converted to a real ES module in v10.9's batch-4 migration, which made its top-level `const JC_KEY` module-scoped instead of implicitly global — but drive.js and supabase.js are still classic (non-module) scripts that reference the bare identifier JC_KEY directly, expecting it on window. Same class of bug as the six pre-existing ones called out in v10.8/v10.9 (a classic-script consumer relying on sloppy-mode global semantics that module scripts don't have), just missed for this specific constant during the batch-4 pass. Fix: added `window.JC_KEY = JC_KEY;` right after its declaration in jazz-cash.js, matching the existing window-bridge pattern used for LEDGER_KEY/CUSTOM_TYPES_KEY etc in ledger-store.js. No other files changed. v10.9: two sessions' worth of changes, neither had bumped this file yet. (a) Housekeeping pass: README.md's stale module-count claims fixed (now sourced by literally grepping index.html rather than hand-counted); js/data-base.js deleted (dead code — MONTHLY_BASE/DAILY_BASE, loaded by no <script> tag, already correctly excluded from APP_SHELL below since v10.3 but never actually deleted from disk); Jazz Cash's one-time migration-into-Ledger UI (banner/button in jazz-cash.js) and its migrateJazzCashToLedger() function (ledger-migration.js) removed now that the migration has actually been run — bt_jazzcash_v2 (JC_KEY) is kept only as drive.js/supabase.js's backup safety net, nothing reads it as a migration source anymore. (b) Module-migration Stage B, batch 4 — the three files that were mutually blocking each other's conversion (manager-page.js, jazz-cash.js, notes-sheets.js) are untangled and all three converted to real ES modules together. The blocker: jazz-cash.js monkey-patched loadManagerPage and notes-sheets.js monkey-patched switchMgrTab, both relying on sloppy-mode global-function semantics that only classic scripts have. Fix: both patches removed; manager-page.js now calls renderJazzCash()/renderNotesSheets() directly instead (guarded with `typeof X === 'function'`, matching its existing style for renderLedgerView etc). [Also corrects a stray claim in the v10.8 note above: custom-sections.js was never actually a patcher of loadManagerPage — checked directly via grep, it doesn't touch it — that was a documentation error carried from an even earlier pass, not a real behavior.] Real bugs found and fixed during this conversion, none pre-existing (i.e. this migration would have introduced all six, not uncovered them): _nsMgsSearch/_nsMgsSort/_nsMgsGroup/_nsNoteSearch/_nsDataSource/_nsDataSearch (all in notes-sheets.js) and _jcTallyDate (jazz-cash.js, 2 call sites) were all assigned directly from inline onclick/onchange/oninput handlers — that HTML always executes in global scope, so once these files' top-level `var`s stopped being implicitly global (module scope instead), those direct assignments would have silently created disconnected `window.*` globals instead of updating the real module state, breaking search/sort/filter UI with no error. Each now routes through a small bridged setter function instead (e.g. `_nsSetDataSource`, `_jcSelectTallyDate`). ai-bridge.js (largest file in the app) also converted in this pass — no patching involved, just needed real imports for Repository/BTDate/LedgerStore/LedgerActions/STAFF/MONTHLY in place of their `typeof` guards; its 3 external consumers (ai-context.js, ai-helpers.js, commandhub-page.js) are unaffected since they call it via bare identifiers backed by its existing window bridges, unchanged. All four newly-converted files' `<script>` tags flipped to type="module" in index.html; no APP_SHELL changes needed (same files, same paths, just a different `type` attribute — the entries below already had these paths correct). v10.8: manager.js (1906-line monolith) split into 9 real ES modules (manager-shared/staff/salary/generic/credit/unmatched/reports/petty/incentive.js) + app-init.js (module — was misplaced inside manager.js despite being the whole app's bootstrap, unrelated to Manager) + manager-page.js (deliberately kept classic — jazz-cash.js/custom-sections.js/notes-sheets.js monkey-patch its functions and rely on sloppy-mode global semantics to do it; see manager-page.js's own header comment). Also added boot-guard.js, which was added to index.html in a previous pass but never added here — same "silently missing offline" risk as every other entry in this changelog. Six real pre-existing bugs found and fixed during the split, none introduced by it: genRowChange/recalcGenRow and recalcCrdEmp were called from inline oninput handlers (Generic Working row edits, 3 Credit Ledger fields) but were never bridged to window at all, throwing ReferenceError on every edit; _salRows_cur/_genRows_cur/_pettyData/_pettyMonth had their window bridge set only once, before any month was ever loaded, so ai-bridge.js's AI-assistant edit commands (and custom-sections.js's petty "copy to next month") silently operated on a stale/empty snapshot after the first real load — same class of bug _crdData_cur had already correctly avoided by re-syncing its bridge on every load, now applied consistently everywhere else. v10.7: module-migration Stage B, batch 3 — app-context.js converted to a real ES module. This one needed three real fixes first, not just imports: (1) getTgts (targets.js) was never bridged to window — also fixed a genuine pre-existing bug in the process, since app-context.js used to check `window.getTgts` specifically, which nothing ever assigned, so ctx.targets silently returned {} always, meaning the AI Assistant's context summary never actually saw real sales targets; every other consumer (analytics.js, hub-actions.js, reports.js, reports-print.js) correctly used the bare identifier and was unaffected. (2) _curPage (storage.js) is deliberately never bridged to window since ui.js reassigns it directly — added a read-only getCurrentPage() getter instead, bridged to window, which doesn't touch that reassignment concern. (3) _nsSFLoad (notes-sheets.js) was never bridged either — fixing this also fixes an identical already-live silent-fallback bug in cover-dashboard.js (converted to a module in an earlier session, same `typeof _nsSFLoad` check, same silent failure). Also replaced app-context.js's `LedgerStore.getAllLedgerTypes()` etc (against a window-only grouped object with no real ES export) with direct imports of the underlying named functions, which do have real exports. v10.6: module-migration Stage B, batch 2 — commandhub.js converted to a real ES module (zero external consumers verified via grep, so this only had to get its own dependencies right). typeof BTSearch/BTFormat/BTDate 'undefined' guards replaced with real imports from those three modules; their duplicate inline fallback implementations (dead code once import is guaranteed to resolve) removed. Actions/Repository already had real module exports, no change needed there. getAppContext (app-context.js, still classic) left as a bare identifier — resolves via that file's existing window bridge. v10.5: module-migration Stage B, batch 1 (bt-format.js, bt-date.js, bt-search.js converted to real ES modules; bt-calc.js deleted — verified zero consumers anywhere in the repo, dead code fully superseded by config.js's own cashSales/creditSales/branchScore/yearlyCAGR). Removed bt-calc.js from APP_SHELL below and from index.html's script tags. Version bumped so already-installed clients drop the now-404 file from cache instead of holding onto it. v10.4: index.html script-order fix — supabase-js CDN tag was loading AFTER the module scripts (cover-dashboard.js/closing-bridge.js/closing-native.js/audit-bridge.js) that call supabase.createClient() at module-load time. Module scripts + defer scripts execute in strict document order regardless of network speed, so `typeof supabase` was 'undefined' on every page load until the 5-min setInterval retry happened to land after the CDN script finally executed — this is why "Waiting for Closing…" kept coming back even after the RLS/Data-API fixes confirmed the data itself was reachable. Moved the supabase-js <script> tag up above those modules. Version bumped (same reason as v10.1/v10.2/v10.3 note below) so already-installed clients actually fetch the corrected index.html instead of keeping the old one cached forever. v10.3: APP_SHELL was missing 8 more real, actively-loaded files — 6 CSS (closing-native.css, closing-book-print.css, audit-native.css, inventory-native.css, excess-working.css, cover-dashboard.css — all real <link> tags in index.html) and 2 JS (excess-working.js, quick-add.js — both real <script defer> tags). Same "reports/features silently do nothing offline or on a flaky connection" symptom as v10.1's fix, just a different batch of files that had been added to index.html without ever being added here. (js/data-base.js was checked too and correctly left out — it defines MONTHLY_BASE/DAILY_BASE but isn't loaded by any <script> tag; it's dead code, not a missing shell file.) v10.2: added Stock Ledger (Audit domain) — css/stockledger.css + js/stockledger.js — a self-contained never-sold/dead-stock/excess-stock analysis tool with its own Supabase panel + JSON upload fallback, deliberately not wired to inventory-bridge.js's inventory_products table (schema mismatch — see index.html's comment above #page-stockledger). v10.1: APP_SHELL was missing 11 files that index.html actually loads, including js/print.js, the ONE print engine every report in the app now funnels through (Sale/Monthly/Yearly/Manager/CommandHub reports all call Print.render()/renderNewTab()). Same-origin requests use networkFirst, so this only broke offline/flaky-connection printing (no cached fallback when the live fetch for print.js failed), matching the "reports just silently do nothing" symptom. Also missing: cover-dashboard.js, closing-bridge.js, closing-native.js, audit-bridge.js, audit-native.js, inventory-bridge.js, inventory-native.js, staff-notes.js, sheets-patch.js, ui-extras.js. All 11 added below, and the version bumped so already-installed clients actually pick up the corrected shell list instead of keeping the old one cached forever.

